# Legacy import working directories (DEPLOYMENT.md section 7a). They hold the
# exported JSONL, which names 444 real proposers and their email addresses,
# and the converted images. This repo is public and mirrors to GitLab, so a
# stray `git add` here would publish student and sponsor PII.
#
# This is a BACKSTOP, not the rule. Since 2026-09-18 that output belongs in
# Box beside the source data (`$OUT` in DEPLOYMENT.md 7a.0) and no import
# should write into the working tree at all. The pattern stays because the
# directories used to live here, and because a rule that lists members by
# name fails the first time someone adds one: this was `legacy-out/` plus
# `live-out/` until a top-up wrote to `new-out/` and fell straight through.
# `.output` is covered separately above.
*-out/
